---
title: Adobo Eggplant
description: Adobo—both a style of preparation as well as the name of a dish—is one of the most widely known foods of the Philippines, often referred to as its national dish.
course: dinner
cuisine: philippine
servings: 2
author: Sohla El-Waylly
source: https://www.bonappetit.com/recipe/eggplant-adobo
prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 25 minutes
tags:
  - philippine
  - dinner
  - stove
---

Slice @eggplant{1%lb}(cut into quarters lengthwise, then cut crosswise into 2"-wide pieces) and place in a medium bowl. Add @sugar{1%tbsp}, @salt{1%tsp}, and @black pepper{0.5%tsp}. Toss to evenly coat eggplant and let sit at room temperature at least 20 minutes and up to 2 hours.

Peel and thinly slice @garlic{8%cloves}. Add @vegetable oil{3%tbsp} and half of garlic to a medium #Dutch oven{} or other heavy pot. Cook over medium-high heat, stirring constantly with a #wooden spoon{}, until light golden and crisp, about 5 minutes. Using a slotted spoon, transfer garlic chips to a plate; season lightly with @salt{}.

Place @ground pork{4%oz} in same pot and break up into small pieces with #wooden spoon{}. Season with @salt{0.25%tsp} and cook, undisturbed, until deeply browned underneath, about 5 minutes. Using slotted spoon, transfer to another plate, leaving fat behind in pot.

Place eggplant on a clean kitchen towel and blot away any moisture the salt has drawn out.

Working in batches and adding more oil if needed, cook eggplant in same pot until lightly browned, about 3 minutes per side. Transfer to plate with pork.

Pour @water{1.5%cups} into pot and scrape up browned bits from bottom with #wooden spoon{}. Add remaining garlic, @coconut vinegar{3%tbsp}, @soy sauce{2%tbsp}, @bay leaves{2}, @black pepper{1%tsp}, and remaining @sugar{1%tbsp}. Bring to a simmer, then return pork and eggplant to pot. Reduce heat to medium-low, partially cover, and simmer until eggplant is tender and silky and sauce is reduced by half, about 20-25 minutes. Taste and season with more @salt{} and @black pepper{} and add a little more @sugar{} if needed.

Top with garlic chips and serve with @cooked white rice{}.
